<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:37:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>No, this video doesn't disprove the 9/11 attack on the south tower of the World Trade Center</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11</link><description>
A former British member of parliament implied that a video filmed from a helicopter on September 11, 2001 shows that no planes actually hit the World Trade Center's south tower, but this claim would be unfounded. The plane that hit the south tower hit the other side of the building, which isn’t visible in the video.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fd9994e-b75e-11f1-ba39-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/september.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fd9994e-b75e-11f1-ba39-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/september.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a9328f4-b75e-11f1-8eb8-591144522fd5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:01:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fd9994e-b75e-11f1-ba39-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/september.jpg">© X</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky accuses Putin of using nationals of 47 countries to fight Ukraine war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky told the UN General Assembly on Wednesday that Russian President Vladimir Putin had enlisted fighters from 47 countries including North Korea, Ghana and India to fight against Ukraine. Zelensky also warned that his forces could target Russian heating and energy facilities in the winter months if Moscow continues to attack Ukraine's energy infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98f242-b782-11f1-acc3-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266647906867.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98f242-b782-11f1-acc3-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266647906867.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13904f1e-b780-11f1-a29c-43d2500850d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:53:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98f242-b782-11f1-acc3-513157f91e8c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266647906867.jpg">© Heather Khalifa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Holy regulation? Pope in Paris to press case for 'disarming' AI</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260923-holy-regulation-pope-in-paris-to-press-case-for-disarming-ai</link><description>
It's all about his high holiness here in France. For weeks already, the nation's been abuzz over the upcoming visit of Leo. From Friday evening mass at Notre Dame Cathedral and mass before 600-thousand faithful in Paris to the pilgrimage city of Lourdes and a trip to Metz, hometown of father of European unity Robert Schuman. A papal visit to France usually draws much attention to the symbiotic love-hate relationship between the church and a secular state of mostly-lapsed Catholics. And yes, there have been grumblings about the visit's cost to taxpayers. But the pushback's relatively muted. This new American pope seems genuinely popular here in France. We'll ask why.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c8c38ec-b779-11f1-92f1-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T092617Z-1132175007-RC2WONAUADS9-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-POPE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c8c38ec-b779-11f1-92f1-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T092617Z-1132175007-RC2WONAUADS9-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-POPE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3edb1cc-b777-11f1-b68c-b3eb364a902d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:44:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'Breakthrough' archeological find could confirm location of Paris's original settlement</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-breakthrough-archeological-find-could-confirm-paris-origins</link><description>
An ancient wall discovered this summer under a hospital in central Paris is thought to be a fragment of city ramparts built by Iron age settlers. Experts say the stone-and-wood structure could confirm the location of the ancient city of Lutetia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d504aa80-b773-11f1-a019-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C94W2ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d504aa80-b773-11f1-a019-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C94W2ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f82d6646-b773-11f1-a994-7d4c056beff6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:19:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d504aa80-b773-11f1-a019-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C94W2ZQ.jpg">© Simon Wohlfahrt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴Live: 'Russia will never stop,' Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky tells UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">2e6b6f64-b779-11f1-afdb-a3d86e1de546</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:05:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years in prison for 2006 sex assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">23cb2a02-b767-11f1-a85f-7d646cd4eb2f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:56:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Disgraced Hollywood mogul Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years for 2006 sex assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault</link><description>
Disgraced movie mogul Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday in another #MeToo reckoning for sexually assaulting a former production assistant in 2006.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a50d81a-b766-11f1-8f22-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266556744346.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a50d81a-b766-11f1-8f22-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266556744346.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8f1acde-b766-11f1-89ca-d94e92a98b7e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:55:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a50d81a-b766-11f1-8f22-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266556744346.jpg">© Barry Williams, The Daily News via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3b7b0ca-b762-11f1-a655-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T143308Z-978379383-RC22PNAAB0P3-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3b7b0ca-b762-11f1-a655-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T143308Z-978379383-RC22PNAAB0P3-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb7ba0cc-b762-11f1-b0e3-c38db18beb93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:49:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3b7b0ca-b762-11f1-a655-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T143308Z-978379383-RC22PNAAB0P3-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg">© Mike Segar, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Backlash against smart glasses grow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/backlash-against-smart-glasses-grow</link><description>
Paris prosecutors say they have opened several investigations after receiving complaints about women allegedly filmed on the street without their consent by people wearing so-called “smart glasses”. Calls are growing across Europe for action against what campaigners have dubbed “pervert” smart glasses, after secretly filmed footage of women and girls appeared online. Solange Mougin reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27be5fde-b763-11f1-98bc-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-171352-171532-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27be5fde-b763-11f1-98bc-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-171352-171532-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e0aff8c-b763-11f1-bc40-8de92e62c3f4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:30:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US says wants Ukraine, Russia to end strikes on energy sites</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is due to address the UN General Assembly on Wednesday, as US President Donald Trump pushes for an end to Russia’s war and Kyiv seeks to shape renewed diplomatic efforts after more than four and a half years of conflict. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/887b5724-b762-11f1-83fa-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-170742-171323-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/887b5724-b762-11f1-83fa-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-170742-171323-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8da2aedc-b762-11f1-ae44-d3dba34d750f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:25:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelenskyy set to address UN as Russia strikes Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1</link><description>
Russia hammered Ukraine’s capital, Kyiv, with drones in daylight attacks on Wednesday, killing two people and wounding 23, just hours before Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy was due to address world leaders at the UN General Assembly. Zelenskyy met US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, as Trump has expressed frustration over the lack of progress in talks aimed at ending the war and the continued escalation of aerial attacks by both sides. Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cf27816-b761-11f1-8c4c-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-170452-170650-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cf27816-b761-11f1-8c4c-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-170452-170650-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">821b0cf4-b761-11f1-b396-e3532fd6ecbc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:20:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iranian president adresses UNGA amid war with US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iranian-president-adresses-unga-amid-war-with-us</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".  France 24 correspondent from New York, Jessica Le Masurier, tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c1872c8-b761-11f1-b71e-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-170155-170416-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c1872c8-b761-11f1-b71e-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-170155-170416-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">419cd626-b761-11f1-a1b5-1b137aef05aa</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:20:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France in focus</category><title>Why is France's Gen Z turning to Catholicism?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260923-why-is-france-s-gen-z-turning-to-catholicism</link><description>
As France prepares for Pope Leo XIV's visit, a surprising trend has emerged in recent years: the number of baptisms among teenagers and young adults has skyrocketed. More than 21,000 catechumens, those undergoing the period of preparation for baptism into the Christian Church, have been recorded so far in 2026. How can this renewed interest in the Catholic faith be explained? Florence Gaillard reports for France in Focus.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d498365a-b685-11f1-935e-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/FRMG-CEF-EGLISE-260921-2027-Ep-3-transfer.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d498365a-b685-11f1-935e-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/FRMG-CEF-EGLISE-260921-2027-Ep-3-transfer.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3dbe1586-b66e-11f1-b4f5-7bbcd580ac84</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:18:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Florence GAILLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Pope Leo XIV to trace back French ancestry, spiritual roots on visit to France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-pope-leo-xiv-trace-back-french-ancestry-spiritual-roots-visit-to-france</link><description>
Pope Leo’s four-day visit to France, which kicks off on Friday, is something of a homecoming for the Chicago-born pontiff, a grandson of European immigrants with family roots in Normandy. His spiritual roots in French Catholicism run deeper still.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf43a75a-b5ba-11f1-8c04-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/pape-normandie.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf43a75a-b5ba-11f1-8c04-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/pape-normandie.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1752efa-b744-11f1-999e-b50ade0e45b3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:02:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf43a75a-b5ba-11f1-8c04-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/pape-normandie.jpg">© Studio graphique FMM</source><dc:creator>Stéphanie TROUILLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>El Nino: Climate scientists warn of "Godzilla-level" climate event</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-el-nino-climate-scientists-warn-of-godzilla-level-climate-event</link><description>
Extreme heat caused by this year’s “super El Niño” could lead to as many as 451,000 excess deaths worldwide in the six months to February 2027, according to researchers at the University of Chicago’s Climate Impact Lab. The number of extremely hot days is expected to rise by 44%, with Nigeria, Indonesia and Sudan among the countries likely to be worst affected. Researchers warn that the impact could extend well beyond the six-month period studied. Carys Garland reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1fe9db2-b75e-11f1-8954-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-164141-164333-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1fe9db2-b75e-11f1-8954-a5615d7a48ac/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-164141-164333-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7f31478-b75e-11f1-83ad-511ac805f395</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:59:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb495ca-b75e-11f1-ab5b-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-162850-163821-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb495ca-b75e-11f1-ab5b-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-162850-163821-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">422ed8b2-b75e-11f1-a0fb-b3e0727eeafd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:57:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8cdb674-b75c-11f1-b426-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-161034-162844-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8cdb674-b75c-11f1-b426-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-161034-162844-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce3c89d2-b75c-11f1-bed7-fb2242db64af</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:44:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Watch live: Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">3019db2a-b75b-11f1-aec7-473a39b48266</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:30:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Film show: Brad Pitt and his dog take on the wilderness in 'Heart of the Beast'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260923-film-show-brad-pitt-and-his-dog-take-on-the-wilderness-in-heart-of-the-beast</link><description>
Eve Jackson and film critic Emma Jones run through this week's new cinema releases in France. Brad Pitt heads into the Alaskan wilderness with his four-legged co-star in "Heart of the Beast". Also, Robert Pattinson takes on a controversial TV host in "Primetime", a new generation discovers "Sense and Sensibility", and Julia Donaldson and Axel Scheffler's "The Scarecrows' Wedding" arrives on the big screen.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/221e1e34-b72c-11f1-a12d-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-HEART-OF-THE-BEAST-EN-frame-555.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/221e1e34-b72c-11f1-a12d-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-HEART-OF-THE-BEAST-EN-frame-555.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">323ed40e-b72a-11f1-9757-ab4876301d31</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:48:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emma JONES</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Super El Niño could cause 451,000 excess deaths worldwide</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-super-el-ni%C3%B1o-could-cause-451-000-excess-deaths-worldwide</link><description>
Extreme heat linked to this year’s “super El Niño” could cause up to 451,000 excess deaths worldwide in the six months to February 2027, according to researchers at the University of Chicago’s Climate Impact Lab. The number of extremely hot days is expected to rise by 44%, with Nigeria, Indonesia and Sudan among the countries likely to be most affected. Researchers warn that the impact could extend well beyond the six-month period studied. Chloe Brimicombe, a climate scientist from the University of Oxford, shares further details about this climate phenomenon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15bfb630-b753-11f1-b8ef-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-150913-151534-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15bfb630-b753-11f1-b8ef-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-150913-151534-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1ad81342-b753-11f1-aa2e-1313c918f8a2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:37:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>How US players are reshaping France and the continent</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260923-how-us-players-are-reshaping-france-and-the-continent</link><description>
In this edition we welcome CNN's correspondent in France, Melissa Bell. Melissa is the author of "Sous l'influence americaine", an investigation into American interference in France and Europe. She tells us about the ways in which American interference is being felt in Europe and France and what we should expect during the 2027 French presidential election campaign.
